+## Revision 11: ordinary fog admission
+
+Immutable source-only revision of v10. The lattice eligibility predicate no longer requires constant fog. Each original scatter occurrence calculates `CalculateTyraFog` from the cached exact clip-space vector and existing fog uniforms immediately before the unchanged `PerformTyraFogClipCheck`. The three-qword cache layout, original occurrence order, original clip history, and every fallback remain intact. The previous hardcoded 255 coefficient is removed from the lattice path. No new named VU registers are introduced. This adds three seven-instruction fog expansions and removes one constant-load instruction; native allocation and rounded full-resident budget must be checked before execution.
+
+Ordinary night v10 has zero candidate activation and its strict rejection is preserved. V11 requires actual-output fog-enabled pairs, including nonconstant fog, before ordinary pricing. Existing v10 fog-disabled probes do not qualify this change. No build or device action accompanies this preparation.
